//? Title: A Categorical VAE with Explicit Gumbel-Softmax Samples
//? Subtitle: Soft training, discrete KL and matched hard inference diagnostics
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Categorical latent variables have discrete samples, so their reconstruction path has no ordinary
argmax derivative. A Gumbel-softmax relaxation supplies a continuous training path while retaining
matched hard samples for diagnosis. This report derives that distinction, checks all score/noise
partials and calibrates4,096 hard draws, then fits four8-way variables on294 unique binary
circle/square images. Twenty-one visible Adam updates and fixed four-draw validation select
epoch3 at temperature0.7. Heldout soft NLL321.932 plus discrete KL3.116 gives surrogate325.048;
the matched hard Monte Carlo negative ELBO is316.523nats/image. Decode(q) and MAP MSE0.11473/
0.10366 are worse than the fitting mean0.04855. Unfiltered soft/hard pairs and all20 uniform
prior codes retain that limitation. The relaxed objective is a biased continuous surrogate,
not an exact discrete ELBO or a KL between Concrete densities.
)
\toc

> Categorical probabilities, relaxed draws and hard samples

[Jang, Gu and Poole's Gumbel-Softmax](https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01144) and
[Maddison, Mnih and Teh's Concrete distribution](https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.00712)
replace a one-hot categorical draw by a differentiable simplex-valued relaxation.
For logits L, supplied independent midpoint uniforms U in(0,1), Gumbels G=−log(−log U),
and positive temperature tau,

$$
q_c=\operatorname{softmax}(L)_c,\qquad
Y_c=\operatorname{softmax}((L+G)/\tau)_c,\qquad
I=\operatorname{argmax}_c(L_c+G_c).
$$
\alttext(Posterior probabilities depend only on logits, relaxed samples also depend on Gumbels and temperature, and hard Gumbel-max indices are independent of positive temperature.)

Hard Gumbel-max gives actual categorical samples. Lower temperature sharpens the soft sample,
but the hard argmax is unchanged. No straight-through estimator is used here: the decoder
trains on soft Y, and hard one-hot decoding is a separate diagnostic. Sampling never occurs
inside a model forward. All noise banks, including Float64 uniforms/Gumbels and Float32 casts,
are explicit native C++ artifacts.

