\image(figures/gumbel_method.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Training follows the continuous soft sample. Hard indices share the same logits/noise, but introduce no argmax derivative into fitting.)
\alttext(Images produce logits and posterior probabilities; explicit Gumbels feed a soft sample and matched hard indices. A shared decoder supplies soft training and separate hard diagnostics, while discrete KL comes from q.)

> A hand-checkable draw and its derivatives

For L=[.1,−.4,.7] and G=[.3,−.2,.6], hard index2 wins for every positive temperature.
At tau=.25 the soft sample is sharp; at tau2 it is diffuse. q remains unchanged.
The softmax Jacobian and the discrete uniform-prior KL are

$$
\frac{\partial Y_i}{\partial L_j}=\frac{\partial Y_i}{\partial G_j}
=\frac1\tau Y_i(\delta_{ij}-Y_j),\qquad
K=\sum_c q_c\log(Cq_c).
$$
\alttext(The relaxation has the same derivative with respect to logits and Gumbels; the posterior KL depends only on logits.)

For A=0.5 sum(Y²)+0.3K, let S=sum(Y²). Then
dA/dG_j=Y_j(Y_j−S)/tau, and dA/dL_j adds0.3q_j[log(Cq_j)−K].
The discrete KL uses q and stable log_softmax(L), not log of an underflowed q.
A zero probability times its finite log-softmax value contributes zero. Float32 uses
source-rounded temperature and log C. Small negative KL roundoff is not clipped.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gumbel_hand.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  const auto t = n::DType::Float64;
  auto       L = n::tensor({.1, -.4, .7}, {1, 3}, t), G = n::tensor({.3, -.2, .6}, {1, 3}, t);
  auto       chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (double tau : {.25, .7, 2.}) {
    const auto o = n::models::GumbelCategorical(L, G, tau);
    if (o.indices.item<std::int64_t>() != 2)
      return 1;
    auto y = o.relaxed.to_vector<double>();
    chart.lines(
        {0, 1, 2},
        y,
        "tau=" + std::to_string(tau),
        tau == .25  ? dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}
        : tau == .7 ? dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}
                    : dm::RGBA{22, 163, 74},
        2);
    std::print(
        "tau {:.2f}: relaxed {}; hard2; q {}.\n",
        tau,
        o.relaxed.values_str(),
        o.probability.values_str());
  }
  chart.title("One explicit Gumbel draw / three temperatures")
      .x_label("category index")
      .y_label("relaxed simplex coordinate")
      .save_svg("build/gumbel_hand.svg");
}
```
