> Soft/hard mismatch and weak reconstruction controls

Epoch3 is selected. Heldout soft NLL321.932229 and discrete KL3.115642 give the relaxed
objective325.047870 nats/image. Hard NLL313.407284 plus the same KL gives the distinct
Monte Carlo discrete negative ELBO316.522925. This difference does not prove that optimizing
the surrogate optimizes the hard likelihood. Decode(q) MSE0.114726214 and MAP MSE0.103664132
are worse than the fitting-only mean0.048548290. A nonlinear decoder's decode(q) and MAP
decode are neither posterior predictive means. Three short epochs and one seed establish
no useful categorical semantics or generative quality.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gumbel_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/gumbel_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::vector<double> epoch, soft, hard;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    std::istringstream row(line);
    double             e, train, a, b, kl, total;
    row >> e >> train >> a >> b >> kl >> total;
    epoch.push_back(e);
    soft.push_back(total);
    hard.push_back(b + kl);
  }
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(epoch, soft, "selected relaxed criterion", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(epoch, hard, "hard MC negative ELBO / diagnostic", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("Fixed four-draw validation: different objectives")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/gumbel_learning.svg");
}
