> Reproduction evidence and native binding scope

All18 original NPZ archives are compared by dtype, shape and every value byte: data/noise,
unit algebra/calibration, first forward/gradients/update, all epochs, selected arrays,
all13 source evaluation fields at every saved draw and the80 prior uniforms/IDs. Batch/source
order and complete histories match exactly. A separate optional NumPy oracle checks all53,104
first derivatives, the first Float32 Adam update, each soft/hard prediction and analytic KL,
all explicit uniform/Gumbel values, calibration frequencies and all three eligible criteria.
It performs no fitting, preparation or downloads.

```
python3 scripts/check_gumbel_categorical_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/gumbel_vae --json build/nn-report-conversion/gumbel_vae/oracle.json
```

Native APIs are GumbelNoise, GumbelCategorical, CategoricalUniformKl, GumbelDecodeSoft,
GumbelDecodeIds and GumbelCategoricalAutoencoder. All floating endpoints and bank fields own
lifetime; hard indices are Int64 in the sampler and Int32 in the full model, and one-hots
match the computation dtype. C++ validates widths, noise, temperatures, simplex sums and IDs
before creating model leaves. Python/R tests cover retained results after collection,
full-uint32 seeds, Float64, live continuous inputs, both target-free decoders and caller-owned
Adam. This API addition does not mark incomplete independent Python/R experiment loops as
native ports. Hard argmax carries no derivative and no straight-through estimator is hidden.
